<Base
  title="Day 0: starting a public build log — bbd.sh notebook"
  description="bbd.sh's first build log entry. We've decided to publish the whole process of doing SEO and brand from zero — real numbers, real progress, real reviews."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="build-meta mb-6">
      #kickoff · #meta
    </div>

    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight mb-8">
      Day 0: starting a public build log
    </h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-ink/60 italic mb-12 border-l-4 border-electric pl-4">
      "How do you know your SEO is working?" — a candidate client asked us last week.
      We decided to stop explaining with slides and just <strong>show the whole thing</strong>.
    </p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/85 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
      <h2>Background — starting from zero</h2>
      <p>
        The bbd.sh domain just went up.
        As we write this, Google doesn't know us and we have no backlinks.
        That's the honest starting line for any new site, and we won't pretend otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>Why publish — not a marketing stunt</h2>
      <p>
        We've done SEO, brand, and growth on different projects over the years —
        always quietly. Then clients had to take our word for it
        based on a few numbers in a deck.
        This time we're trying it differently:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Transparency is marketing</strong> — peers can see what we do and the result. More convincing than any case study.</li>
        <li><strong>It's content in itself</strong> — a real public record gets shared, which earns links naturally.</li>
        <li><strong>It forces us to do it right</strong> — public means no shortcuts.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>What we'll do</h2>
      <p>No grand promises. A short list of directions we'll keep working on:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Cover the technical SEO basics for bbd.sh (schema, sitemap, robots, llms.txt, SSG)</li>
        <li>Get on the radar of Google, Bing, and the AI assistants</li>
        <li>Keep publishing notebook entries — not marketing, build logs</li>
        <li>Build out brand entities (Wikidata, social consistency, Crunchbase, etc.)</li>
        <li>Publish real progress numbers regularly</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we won't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No bulk AI-generated content</li>
        <li>No paid backlinks / no PBNs</li>
        <li>No keyword stuffing</li>
        <li>No SERP CTR manipulation</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <p>
        We'll keep posting notebook updates at a steady cadence and quality.
        Each entry: what we did this period, the real numbers, what's next.
        Subscribe to the newsletter or follow <a href="https://x.com/bbd_sh" class="text-electric">@bbd_sh</a> if you want to track it.
      </p>

      <p class="font-display text-2xl italic text-ink/70 mt-12 border-l-4 border-electric pl-6">
        "Watch us build. Win or lose — we'll publish either way."
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="my-16 border-ink/10" />

    <a href="/notebook" class="inline-block font-mono text-sm text-ink hover:text-electric">
      ← all entries
    </a>
